Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has at least one order in `New` status created within the last 7 days, AND at least one order in a DIFFERENT status (e.g. Processing or Cancelled) also created within the last 7 days, AND at least one `New`-status order OLDER than 7 days (outside the window) — this proves the window boundary, not just presence. Per VCST-5587's confirmed implementation: value = New-status orders in the rolling 7-day window; delta = ALL-status order volume of that SAME window (not a percent-change indicator).

Assertions:
[DOM] the 'New orders' card's primary value equals the COUNT of @td(ORG_ACME.id)'s orders in `New` status created within the last 7 days — an order in any OTHER status within the same window is excluded from this count {SPEC}
[DOM] the 'New orders' card's sub-value is the money TOTAL of that same New-only order set {SPEC}
[DOM] the 'New orders' card's delta/secondary figure is the ALL-status order volume of the SAME rolling 7-day window — not a New-only count, not a percent-change indicator {SPEC}
[STATE] a `New`-status order older than 7 days does NOT move either figure {SPEC}
[STATE] an order carrying the `IsCancelled`/`IsPrototype` FLAG (not merely a `Cancelled` STATUS) is excluded from BOTH figures, while an order whose STATUS is literally `Cancelled` still counts toward the all-status delta figure {SPEC}

Cross_Layer_Checks:
[API] salesRepCustomerOrderStatistics(organizationId: @td(ORG_ACME.id), period: {recentFrom, recentTo}, filter: "New") count/total match the card's value/sub, errors[] empty {SPEC}
[API] the SAME query with no status filter, same window, returns the count backing the delta figure {SPEC}
[NETWORK] no 4xx/5xx on the statistics request

